course: dictionary
lesson: 8059
title: Reject: saying no
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To reject something is to refuse to accept it, take it or agree to it. «The machine rejected the bent coin» means the machine would not take the coin.
explain: You can also reject a person. To reject someone is to refuse to include them or to love them. «Feel rejected» means you feel turned away or left out, and that hurts. Lessons about friendship teach us how to include others.
explain: Reject can also be a noun. A reject is something thrown out because it is faulty, or a person who has been turned away. Look at the words around it to find out which one is meant.
explain: Clues help you. «Historians reject this because there is no evidence» tells you why they say no: the evidence is missing. Swap in refuse to accept and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Reject» means to refuse to accept, take or agree to something.
fact: «Feel rejected» means feel turned away or left out.
fact: A «reject» is something thrown out because it is faulty.
fact: In a letter about a job or a place, «unsuccessful» means rejected.
fact: Phrases to learn: «reject an offer», «reject an idea».
exercise: «The machine rejected the bent coin.» What does rejected mean here? | *Refused to take | Painted bright red | Counted twice | Happily hugged
exercise: «Historians reject this because there is no evidence.» What does reject mean here? | Lose it on purpose | *Refuse to accept, because the proof is missing | Copy it carefully | Agree with it completely
exercise: In «The shop sold the rejects cheaply», what are the rejects? | Free sweets | *Faulty things thrown out | Heavy boxes | Brand-new bikes
test: Mia felt rejected when she was not picked for the team. What does this mean? | She felt proud and tall | *She felt turned away and left out | She felt sleepy after lunch | She felt cold on the pitch
test: «Most birds will not reject a chick that a person touched.» What does reject mean? | *Turn it away and refuse to care for it | Feed it bread at lunchtime | Sing a song to it | Pick it up and carry it home
exam: In «The letter said his application was unsuccessful», what does unsuccessful mean? | Written in pencil | Delayed by the post | Accepted with a prize | *Rejected
